<h2 class='date-header'><span>08/09/2026</span></h2>

          <div class="date-posts">
        
<div class='post-outer'>
<div class='post hentry uncustomized-post-template' itemprop='blogPost' itemscope='itemscope' itemtype='http://schema.org/BlogPosting'>
<meta content='5107039156280592857' itemprop='blogId'/>
<meta content='4341945275509102330' itemprop='postId'/>
<a name='4341945275509102330'></a>
<h3 class='post-title entry-title' itemprop='name'>
<a href='https://cryptiana.blogspot.com/2026/09/wellingtons-codecipher-during.html'>Wellington's Code/Cipher during the Peninsular War</a>
</h3>
<div class='post-header'>
<div class='post-header-line-1'></div>
</div>
<div class='post-body entry-content' id='post-body-4341945275509102330' itemprop='description articleBody'>
<p>Some months ago, I wrote about <a href="https://cryptiana.blogspot.com/2026/04/a-british-book-cipher-during-american.html">a British book cipher</A> during the American Revolutionary War. This time, I uploaded a new article about Wellington's dictionary code: <a href="https://cryptiana.web.fc2.com/code/maitland.htm">"Wellington's Polyalphabetic Cipher with a Dictionary Code"</A>. For words/names not found in the dictionary, a polyalphabetic cipher with heavy nulls was used.</p>
<p>My observations are based on Wellington's despatch to General Maitland dated 2 September 1812. I thank George Lasry for the information of the auction of the letter at <a href="https://live.spink.com/lots/view/4-ML16CI/great-britain-duke-of-wellington-peninsular-war-etc-general-frederick-maitland-1763-1848-17">Spink</A>.</p>
<div style='clear: both;'></div>
</div>
<div class='post-footer'>
<div class='post-footer-line post-footer-line-1'>
